<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Type" DataType="STRING_16" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Type identifier for HMI navigation]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>07 00 00 00 50 5F 4C 6F 67 69 63 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="7">
<![CDATA['P_Logic']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Tag" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tagname for display on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>07 00 00 00 50 5F 4C 6F 67 69 63 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="7">
<![CDATA['P_Logic']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_Label" DataType="STRING_20" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Label for graphic symbol displayed on HMI]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>12 00 00 00 43 6F 6E 66 69 67 75 72 61 62 6C 65 
20 4C 6F 67 69 63 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="18">
<![CDATA['Configurable Logic']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_DateTime" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="7" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Date/Time Stamp from scan of logic]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<Array DataType="DINT" Dimensions="7" Radix="Decimal">
<Element Index="[0]" Value="0"/>
<Element Index="[1]" Value="0"/>
<Element Index="[2]" Value="0"/>
<Element Index="[3]" Value="0"/>
<Element Index="[4]" Value="0"/>
<Element Index="[5]" Value="0"/>
<Element Index="[6]" Value="0"/>
</Array>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Cfg_NavTag" DataType="STRING_20" Dimensions="8" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tagnames for destinations of Navigation buttons]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="0">
<![CDATA['']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Lib" DataType="STRING_12" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Library for Faceplate call-up]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 52 41 2D 42 41 53 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['RA-BAS']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Set Output to False and reset On-Delay and Off-Delay output timers]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================

If this instruction is OFF-SCAN (rung is false or EnableIn is false in FBD),
then set the Output to FALSE (0) and reset the Output TON and TOF timers.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out_Live)RES(Wrk_OnDelayT)RES(Wrk_OffDelayT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Examine Inputs and execute Logic Gates and Output timers]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_Logic:  PROCESS -- BOOLEAN LOGIC
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Added Cfg_HasNav bits and
Cfg_NavTag strings for navigation
V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Unmodified for Library of Process Objects V3.1, up-rev only.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed On-Delay and Off-Delay timers ACC/PRE (read-only).
============================================================
This Instruction executes logic on up to 8 input conditions.
It provides these features:

*  Up to eight 4-source logic gates can be used.
*  Each of the gates can be configured as:

-  an AND Gate(result true if ALL sources are true)
-  an OR Gate (result true if ANY source is true)
-  an XOR (exclusive OR) Gate (result true if an ODD number of sources are true)
-  a Majority (1oo1: 2oo2, 2oo3 or 3oo4) Voting Gate (result true if a majority of sources are true)
-  a Set-Reset (Latch) Gate (result turned ON by Set source, turned OFF by Reset source)
-  a Select Gate (result = Source A if selector false, Source B if true)

* Each of the 4 sources for each gate can be configured to be
any of the instruction's inputs or any gate's result.
* Each of the 4 sources for each gate can be enabled or disabled
and can be optionally inverted (logical NOT).
* Any input or gate result can be selected, and optionally inverted,
as the source for the instruction output 
* The output has OnDelay and OffDelay timers; the output bit is set when
the source for the output is true for the OnDelay time; the
output is cleared when the source is false for the OffDelay time.
* A status register is updated with the states of all inputs and gate results.
* Snapshot registers capture the instruction state either when the Output
goes to its configured "snap state", on Command, or when
Inp_Hold  input is true (configurable) (for example, for capture
for Root Cause Failure Analysis of Interlocks).  The snapshot can be
configured for "snap first" requiring a reset before the next snapshot
can be taked, or "snap over" ("snap last") where a snapshot is
captured with each snapshot condition  (without reset).

Configuration Error Rules:
*   If a gate has no gate type selected (function code = 0), no error is flagged
(NULL gate) and its Result bit is cleared.
*   If a gate has an invalid function code, an error (function code) is flagged and
the Result bit is held in its last state.
*   If a gate has an invalid source pointer, an error (source pointer) is flagged and
the Result bit is held in its last state.
*   If a gate has a valid function code but no sources enabled (used), an error
(sources used) is flagged and the Result bit is held in its last state.
*   For Set/Reset, at least one of the Set sources and at least one of the Reset
sources must be used.
*   For Selector, source 3 (the select) must be used and at least one of the
A (source 1) or B (source 2) sources must be used.
*   All other gates can have any number of sources used from 1 to 4.
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Cfg_NavTag strings on this rung  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)[CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag) ,LOWER(Cfg_0StText,Cfg_1StText) LOWER(Cfg_InpTxt[0],Cfg_InpTxt[1]) LOWER(Cfg_InpTxt[2],Cfg_InpTxt[3]) LOWER(Cfg_InpTxt[4],Cfg_InpTxt[5]) LOWER(Cfg_InpTxt[6],Cfg_InpTxt[7]) ,LOWER(Cfg_NavTag[0],Cfg_NavTag[1]) LOWER(Cfg_NavTag[2],Cfg_NavTag[3]) LOWER(Cfg_NavTag[4],Cfg_NavTag[5]) LOWER(Cfg_NavTag[6],Cfg_NavTag[7]) LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INP_HOLD SNAPSHOT: PREVIOUS SCAN'S DATA
============================================================
If the Inp_Hold bit becomes set, and if the Inp_Hold bit is
configured to be used to take a snapshot, and if we don't already
have a snapshot or snapshot overwrite (last snap) is configured,
copy the live state FROM LAST SCAN to the snapshot state
(including last scan's timestamp).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)XIC(Inp_Hold)ONS(Wrk_InpHoldONS)XIO(S:FS)XIC(Cfg_UseInpHold)[XIO(Wrk_SnapLatch) ,XIC(Cfg_SnapOver) ][MOV(5,Val_SnapInit) OTL(Wrk_SnapLatch) ,XIC(Sts_OutInvLive) OTL(Sts_OutInvSnap) ,XIO(Sts_OutInvLive) OTU(Sts_OutInvSnap) ,XIC(Out_Live) OTL(Out_Snap) ,XIO(Out_Live) OTU(Out_Snap) ,MOV(Val_DelayPctLive,Val_DelayPctSnap) ,MOV(Sts_InpLive,Sts_InpSnap) MOV(Sts_GateLive,Sts_GateSnap) ,MOV(Sts_GateSrc1Live,Sts_GateSrc1Snap) MOV(Sts_GateSrc2Live,Sts_GateSrc2Snap) ,MOV(Sts_GateSrc3Live,Sts_GateSrc3Snap) MOV(Sts_GateSrc4Live,Sts_GateSrc4Snap) ,XIC(Cfg_TSonSnap) COP(Wrk_DateTime[0],Val_SnapTS[0],7) ,OTU(Wrk_Copy) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INPUT GATHERING
============================================================
This object uses pointerized, looping logic.  The individual
Condition Inputs are aliased together into an 8-bit word
for indirect referencing (by bit #).  No rungs needed for gathering.
============================================================
LOOP THROUGH THE GATES
============================================================
Set up a loop for the 8 Gates.
Clear the "last gate" values used for HMI faceplate animation.
Clear the flags for errors detected in configuration, and
set the loop index to start with the first Gate (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Wrk_LastGate[0],16)CLR(Wrk_M)CLR(Wrk_ErrFunc)CLR(Wrk_ErrGateSrcPtr)CLR(Wrk_ErrMask);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
TOP OF LOOP, PER GATE
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
For this gate:
* Set a pointer to the bit in Sts that receives the result of this gate.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(NextGate)ADD(Wrk_M,8,Wrk_Mplus8);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[* Check the Gate function code:
- If it's zero, the gate is not used (null).  Clear the result and skip to the next gate
- If it's invalid, flag the error, hold the result in its last state, and skip to the next gate.
* Check the Gate Source Pointers:
- If any are invalid, flag the error, hold the result in its last state and skip to the next gate.
* Check the Gate Source Used Flags:
- If a used (non null) gate has NO sources used, flag the error, hold the result
in its last state and skip to the next gate.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],0) OTU(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,LIM(7,Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],-1) OTL(Wrk_ErrFunc.[Wrk_M]) ,[LIM(16,Cfg_GateSrc1Ptr[Wrk_M],-1) ,LIM(16,Cfg_GateSrc2Ptr[Wrk_M],-1) ,LIM(16,Cfg_GateSrc3Ptr[Wrk_M],-1) ,LIM(16,Cfg_GateSrc4Ptr[Wrk_M],-1) ] OTL(Wrk_ErrGateSrcPtr.[Wrk_M]) ,NEQ(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],0) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) OTL(Wrk_ErrMask.[Wrk_M]) ]JMP(EndGate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy this Gate's Source Pointers to working registers.
(We need to do this because Logix only lets us indirect one thing at a time!)

Once we have the pointers to the Sources, we can update the "Last Gate" registers
used to animate lines in the HMI Popup with "how far" to draw them for each input and gate.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(Cfg_GateSrc3Ptr[Wrk_M],Wrk_Src3Ptr) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) CPT(Wrk_LastGate[Wrk_Src3Ptr],Wrk_M*4+1) ,MOV(Cfg_GateSrc2Ptr[Wrk_M],Wrk_Src2Ptr) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) CPT(Wrk_LastGate[Wrk_Src2Ptr],Wrk_M*4+2) ,MOV(Cfg_GateSrc4Ptr[Wrk_M],Wrk_Src4Ptr) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) CPT(Wrk_LastGate[Wrk_Src4Ptr],Wrk_M*4+3) ,MOV(Cfg_GateSrc1Ptr[Wrk_M],Wrk_Src1Ptr) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) CPT(Wrk_LastGate[Wrk_Src1Ptr],Wrk_M*4+4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles gathering the pointed-to Sts bits
and inverting them if so configured.

The actual Source state for each Source on each Gate (before inversion)
is saved in a Status for use by the HMI Popup Display.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src1Ptr]) OTE(Sts_GateSrc1Live.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc1Inv.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src1Ptr]) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Inv.[Wrk_M]) ] OTE(Wrk_Src1) ,[XIC(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src2Ptr]) OTE(Sts_GateSrc2Live.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc2Inv.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src2Ptr]) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Inv.[Wrk_M]) ] OTE(Wrk_Src2) ,[XIC(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src3Ptr]) OTE(Sts_GateSrc3Live.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc3Inv.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src3Ptr]) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc3Inv.[Wrk_M]) ] OTE(Wrk_Src3) ,[XIC(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src4Ptr]) OTE(Sts_GateSrc4Live.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc4Inv.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Src4Ptr]) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Inv.[Wrk_M]) ] OTE(Wrk_Src4) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Function Code = 5:  SET - RESET
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

NOTE:  THIS FUNCTION IS PROCESSED FIRST
(and Function Code 6, Selector, is processed second)
BECAUSE ITS RESULT STATE IS LATCHED.
IF THIS FUNCTION IS USED, THE JMP AT THE END
KEEPS THE OTE's IN THE OTHER FUNCTIONS,
BELOW, FROM CLEARING THE LATCHED RESULT INADVERTANTLY!

This Function requires at least one "Set" Source (Source 1 or 3) and
at least one "Reset" Source (Source 2 or 4).
If both "Set" Sources are not used, or if both "Reset" Sources are
not used, flag an error and leave the gate Result in its last state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],5)[XIO(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) ]OTL(Wrk_ErrMask.[Wrk_M])JMP(EndGate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set - Reset Logic

The S-R has a dominant Set (1) and Reset (2) Source, and a Non-Dominant
Set (3) and Reset (4) Source, allowing consturction of either a
Set-Dominant or Reset-Dominant Set-Reset Gate.
For each pair, the first one received wins, and the Dominant pair
wins over the Non-Dominant pair.

If the Non-Dominant Set Source is True and NEITHER Reset Source is True,
Set (OTL) the Result.
If the Non-Dominant Reset Source is True and NEITHER Set Source is True,
Clear (OTU) the Result.
If the Dominant Set Source is True and the Dominant Reset Source is False,
Set (OTL) the Result.
If the Dominant Reset Source is True and the Dominant Set Source is False,
Clear (OTU) the Result.
Otherwise, the Result maintains its last state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],5)[XIC(Wrk_Src3) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) [XIO(Wrk_Src2) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] [XIO(Wrk_Src4) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] OTL(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,XIC(Wrk_Src4) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) [XIO(Wrk_Src1) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] [XIO(Wrk_Src3) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] OTU(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,XIC(Wrk_Src1) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) [XIO(Wrk_Src2) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] OTL(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,XIC(Wrk_Src2) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) [XIO(Wrk_Src1) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] OTU(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,JMP(EndGate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Function Code = 6  A/B Selector
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

This Function requires that the Select (#3) source is used and AT LEAST ONE of
its A / B sources (#1 or #2) is used.  Source #4 must be UNUSED.

If source #3 is not used, if source #1 and #2 are BOTH unused, or if source #4 IS used,
flag the error and leave the gate result in its last state.

This Function selects either the A Source (#1) or the B Source (#2)
to pass through as its result, depending on the state of the A/B Select Source (#3).
If the A/B Select is FALSE (after inversion), pass through Source A (after inversion).
If the A/B Select is TRUE (after inversion), pass through Source B (after inversion).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],6)[[XIO(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) XIO(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] OTL(Wrk_ErrMask.[Wrk_M]) JMP(EndGate) ,[XIO(Wrk_Src3) XIC(Wrk_Src1) ,XIC(Wrk_Src3) XIC(Wrk_Src2) ] OTE(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,JMP(EndGate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Function Code = 1:  LOGICAL   "AND"
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

If all of the "Used" Sources are true, this gate's Result is true.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],1)[[XIC(Wrk_Src1) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] [XIC(Wrk_Src2) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] [XIC(Wrk_Src3) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] [XIC(Wrk_Src4) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIO(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] OTE(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,JMP(EndGate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Function Code = 2:  LOGICAL   "OR"
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

If any of the "Used" Sources are true, this gate's Result is true.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],2)[[XIC(Wrk_Src1) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIC(Wrk_Src2) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIC(Wrk_Src3) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) ,XIC(Wrk_Src4) XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) ] OTE(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,JMP(EndGate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Logical Exclusive OR (XOR) and Majority (M out of N or "MooN") gates
need to know how many Sources are Used
and how many of the Used Sources are True (after input inverting).

Clear the totals, then add the numbers for each Source Used and True.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcsUsed) CLR(Wrk_SrcsTrue) ,XIC(Cfg_GateSrc1Mask.[Wrk_M]) [ADD(Wrk_SrcsUsed,1,Wrk_SrcsUsed) ,XIC(Wrk_Src1) ADD(Wrk_SrcsTrue,1,Wrk_SrcsTrue) ] ,XIC(Cfg_GateSrc2Mask.[Wrk_M]) [ADD(Wrk_SrcsUsed,1,Wrk_SrcsUsed) ,XIC(Wrk_Src2) ADD(Wrk_SrcsTrue,1,Wrk_SrcsTrue) ] ,XIC(Cfg_GateSrc3Mask.[Wrk_M]) [ADD(Wrk_SrcsUsed,1,Wrk_SrcsUsed) ,XIC(Wrk_Src3) ADD(Wrk_SrcsTrue,1,Wrk_SrcsTrue) ] ,XIC(Cfg_GateSrc4Mask.[Wrk_M]) [ADD(Wrk_SrcsUsed,1,Wrk_SrcsUsed) ,XIC(Wrk_Src4) ADD(Wrk_SrcsTrue,1,Wrk_SrcsTrue) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Function Code = 3:  LOGICAL "EXCLUSIVE OR" (XOR)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

If more Sources True than are Used, something is amiss.  Flag the error and hold last state.

Of the Used sources, the XOR result is true if an ODD number of them (1 or 3) are True.

(This Function will likely be most often used with TWO Sources.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],3)[LES(Wrk_SrcsUsed,Wrk_SrcsTrue) OTL(Wrk_ErrMask.[Wrk_M]) JMP(EndGate) ,[EQU(Wrk_SrcsTrue,1) ,EQU(Wrk_SrcsTrue,3) ] OTE(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,JMP(EndGate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Function Code = 4:  M out of N (MooN, Majority)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

If more Sources True than are Used, something is amiss.  Flag the error and hold last state.

This Function's Result is True when a MAJORITY of its used Sources are true.

The Result is true when:

if one Source is Used, when that Source is true;
if two or three Sources are Used, when at least two are true;
if four Sources are Used, when at lest three are true.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Cfg_GateFunc[Wrk_M],4)[LES(Wrk_SrcsUsed,Wrk_SrcsTrue) OTL(Wrk_ErrMask.[Wrk_M]) JMP(EndGate) ,[EQU(Wrk_SrcsUsed,1) GEQ(Wrk_SrcsTrue,1) ,LIM(2,Wrk_SrcsUsed,3) GEQ(Wrk_SrcsTrue,2) ,EQU(Wrk_SrcsUsed,4) GEQ(Wrk_SrcsTrue,3) ] OTE(Wrk_Src.[Wrk_Mplus8]) ,JMP(EndGate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
BOTTOM OF LOOP, PER GATE
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Processing of this Gate is complete.
If this was not the last Gate, increment the Loop Index (Wrk_M)
and go back to process the next Gate.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(EndGate)LES(Wrk_M,7)ADD(Wrk_M,1,Wrk_M)JMP(NextGate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PROCESS THE OUTPUT
============================================================
The Output has OnDelay and OffDelay Timers applied to the selected input/gate Result.

* Multiply the configured presets in Seconds by 1000 to get milliseconds for the Timer Presets.
* Check the Presets for validity; if not valid (negative), clear and flag the error.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MUL(Cfg_OnDelay,1000,Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE) MUL(Cfg_OffDelay,1000,Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE) ,[LES(Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE,0) CLR(Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE) ,LES(Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE,0) CLR(Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE) ] OTE(Err_Timer) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Check the Output Source Pointer to make sure it points to a valid
AOI Input (0 to 7) or Gate Result (8 to 15).
If not, flag the error and skip evaluation of the result (to avoid a major fault)
and reset the Output OnDelay and OffDelay Timers.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIM(16,Cfg_OutSrcPtr,-1)OTE(Wrk_ErrOutSrcPtr)RES(Wrk_OnDelayT)RES(Wrk_OffDelayT)JMP(Output);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Update the "last gate" values used in animating the HMI Popup with which
gate or input is tied to the output so a line can be drawn to the output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(33,Wrk_LastGate[Cfg_OutSrcPtr]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Output Source Pointer is valid, de-reference it and grab the pointed-to bit,
invert it if so configured, and if that result is true, note it.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_OutSrcInv) XIC(Wrk_Src.[Cfg_OutSrcPtr]) ,XIC(Cfg_OutSrcInv) XIO(Wrk_Src.[Cfg_OutSrcPtr]) ]OTE(Sts_OutInvLive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Output OnDelay and OffDelay Timers follow the logic result to generate the final output.

@@@@@  The TON on each branch is doubled to ensure its .DN bit is  @@@@@
@@@@@  set or cleared the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_OutInvLive)[TON(Wrk_OnDelayT,?,?) TON(Wrk_OnDelayT,?,?) ,TOF(Wrk_OffDelayT,?,?) TOF(Wrk_OffDelayT,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the OnDelay Timer goes DONE, or if the timer's input is true and its Preset is zero, set the Output.
If the OffDelay Timer is TIMING and its preset is nonzero, set the Output.

(The extra branch and comparisons against the Presets are needed to ensure there is
no one-scan delay in the DN bit of the TON or the timing of the TOF affecting the Output.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Output)[XIC(Sts_OutInvLive) XIC(Wrk_OnDelayT.DN) OTL(Out_Live) ,XIO(Sts_OutInvLive) XIO(Wrk_OffDelayT.DN) OTU(Out_Live) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
GENERATE VALUES AND STATUS
============================================================
This rung generates the OnDelay / OffDelay "percent complete" value
for the HMI progress bar for output delay.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_OnDelayT.TT) GRT(Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE,0) CPT(Val_DelayPctLive,Wrk_OnDelayT.ACC*100/Wrk_OnDelayT.PRE) ,XIC(Wrk_OffDelayT.TT) GRT(Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE,0) CPT(Val_DelayPctLive,Wrk_OffDelayT.ACC*100/Wrk_OffDelayT.PRE) ,[XIO(Wrk_OnDelayT.TT) XIO(Wrk_OffDelayT.TT) ,XIC(Sts_OutInvLive) XIC(Out_Live) ,XIO(Sts_OutInvLive) XIO(Out_Live) ] MOV(100,Val_DelayPctLive) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates the gate-wise Err_xxx configuration error bits]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Wrk_ErrFunc,Err_GateFunc)MOV(Wrk_ErrGateSrcPtr,Err_GateSrcPtr)MOV(Wrk_ErrMask,Err_GateSrcMask);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates the remaining Err_xxx configuration error bits and
summarizes them all Err_ params into Sts_Err (summary configuration error status bit).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(Err_GateFunc,0) ,NEQ(Err_GateSrcPtr,0) ,NEQ(Err_GateSrcMask,0) ,XIC(Wrk_ErrOutSrcPtr) OTE(Err_OutSrcPtr) ,XIC(Err_Timer) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung copies out the various Statuses and Values associated with Inputs and Gates:
Current State (Sts_Inp and Sts_Gate) and values used in HMI animation (Val_LastInp, Val_LastGate).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[BTD(Wrk_Src,0,Sts_InpLive,0,8)BTD(Wrk_Src,8,Sts_GateLive,0,8)COP(Wrk_LastGate[0],Val_LastInp[0],8)COP(Wrk_LastGate[8],Val_LastGate[0],8);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
GENERATE SNAPSHOT
============================================================
The following rungs generate the logic snapshot used to display the
"shutdown cause" when this instruction is used for complex interlock logic (for example).

This rung sets us up to copy current logic status data to the snapshot area this scan.
If there has been no snapshot since last reset, plan on copying the live data to
the snap shot this scan.

NOTE:  All the methods below of triggering a snapshot will copy data THIS scan's state.
Inp_Hold, which is checked at the top of this routine, captures LAST scan's state!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_SnapLatch)OTL(Wrk_Copy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Capture this scan's timestamp.  (We may need it next scan if Inp_Hold comes true...)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[GSV(WALLCLOCKTIME,,LocalDateTime,Wrk_DateTime[0]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung looks for a Snapshot command (Operator or Program) or
for a 0-to-1 or 1-to-0 transition of the Output, or the Inp_Hold Input
to initiate a snapshot.

Note that the snapshot data are THIS scan's logic output, except for
Inp_Hold trigger, which uses LAST scan's logic results!

Record which initiator triggered the snapshot.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Snap) OTU(OCmd_Snap) XIC(Cfg_UseOCmd) [XIO(Wrk_SnapLatch) ,XIC(Cfg_SnapOver) ] MOV(1,Val_SnapInit) ,XIC(PCmd_Snap) OTU(PCmd_Snap) ONS(Wrk_PCmdSnapONS) XIC(Cfg_UsePCmd) [XIO(Wrk_SnapLatch) ,XIC(Cfg_SnapOver) ] MOV(2,Val_SnapInit) ,XIC(Out_Live) ONS(Wrk_Out01SnapONS) XIC(Cfg_UseOut01) [XIO(Wrk_SnapLatch) ,XIC(Cfg_SnapOver) ] MOV(3,Val_SnapInit) ,XIO(Out_Live) ONS(Wrk_Out10SnapONS) XIC(Cfg_UseOut10) [XIO(Wrk_SnapLatch) ,XIC(Cfg_SnapOver) ] MOV(4,Val_SnapInit) ]OTL(Wrk_SnapLatch)OTL(Wrk_Copy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If we don't have a snapshot (show live), or if we need to copy the live data
to the snapshot because we just TOOK the snapshot,
copy the live state to the snapshot state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Copy)[XIC(Sts_OutInvLive) OTL(Sts_OutInvSnap) ,XIO(Sts_OutInvLive) OTU(Sts_OutInvSnap) ,XIC(Out_Live) OTL(Out_Snap) ,XIO(Out_Live) OTU(Out_Snap) ,MOV(Val_DelayPctLive,Val_DelayPctSnap) ,MOV(Sts_InpLive,Sts_InpSnap) MOV(Sts_GateLive,Sts_GateSnap) ,MOV(Sts_GateSrc1Live,Sts_GateSrc1Snap) MOV(Sts_GateSrc2Live,Sts_GateSrc2Snap) ,MOV(Sts_GateSrc3Live,Sts_GateSrc3Snap) MOV(Sts_GateSrc4Live,Sts_GateSrc4Snap) ,XIC(Cfg_TSonSnap) COP(Wrk_DateTime[0],Val_SnapTS[0],7) ,OTU(Wrk_Copy) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND PROCESSING
============================================================
On receipt of a Reset Command, the snapshot is returned to showing live data
and the record of what initiated the snapshot is cleared.

NOTE:  This object is "Modeless" -- Operator and Program Commands
are accepted at any time.  However, Program Reset will only be
accepted if Program Snap is enabled.  Operator Reset (button on
faceplate) is always available (enabled if snapped).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PCmd_Reset) OTU(PCmd_Reset) XIC(Cfg_UsePCmd) ,XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ,XIO(Inp_Hold) XIC(Cfg_UseInpHold) ]OTU(Wrk_SnapLatch)CLR(Val_SnapInit);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Our internal Snapshot latch is copied out to a "Snapped" status.
(Using the Wrk bit prevents logic or the HMI from writing to the Sts bit unintentionally.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_SnapLatch)OTE(Sts_Snapped);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND READIES
============================================================
Snapshot Operator Command button is enabled if there is no snapshot
currently, or Snap Over is allowed, AND Operator Snapshot is enabled in config.

Operator Reset is enabled any time there's a snapshot.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIO(Wrk_SnapLatch) ,XIC(Cfg_SnapOver) ] XIC(Cfg_UseOCmd) OTE(Rdy_Snap) ,XIC(Wrk_SnapLatch) OTE(Rdy_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Reset On-Delay and Off-Delay timers, clear snapshot timestamp and internal data, clear "lurking" commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
Clear all DINTs used as pointers / loop counters to ensure no
"bad index/pointer" Major Fault on powerup.
Clear the Snapshot Timestamp to indicate we haven't taken a snapshot yet.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_M)CLR(Wrk_Mplus8)FLL(0,Val_SnapTS[0],7);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear any "lurking" Commands so they don't trigger on first scan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(PCmd_Snap)OTU(OCmd_Snap)OTU(PCmd_Reset)OTU(OCmd_Reset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_8"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
<WallClockTime Use="Reference">
</WallClockTime>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
